[ti:Day 15]

[00:00.00]clause [klɔːz]n. 条款 例 We should include an arbitration clause in the contract.
[00:07.92]policymaker [ˈpɒləsimeɪkə(r)]n. 政策制定者；决策人
[00:12.60]scam [skæm]n. 花招；骗局 v. 欺诈 例 There is fortunately no need for new regulat ions to crack down on such irresponsible lending practices.
[00:25.80]float [fləʊt]vt. 发行(公债等)；筹(款)；开办公司；实 行计划 vi. 流通；浮动，漂浮 例 The new currency would float to a lower level against the Euro. 搭 float about 传播 / float upward 上浮
[00:41.16]rebalance [riˈbæləns]n./vt. 再平衡；调整
[00:45.00]refrain [rɪˈfreɪn]vi. 制止；克制；避免 例 Please refrain from smoking and talking loudly during the meeting. 搭 refrain from 忍住不做…
[00:57.36]lean [liːn]a. (公司、企业等)得利少的；收益差的；贫 乏的，歉收的 v. (使)倾斜；(使)依靠 例 This lean project cut down the company's gross income. 搭 lean on 依赖，依靠；威胁 / lean over backwards 竭尽全力；矫枉过正
[01:14.04]sequential [sɪˈkwenʃl]a. 连续的；顺序的
[01:17.64]exploit [ɪkˈsplɔɪt]vt. 剥削；利用；开发，开采 [ˈeksplɔɪt]n. [常pl.] 业绩，功绩 例 It's recommended to exploit the particular advantages of each region.
[01:31.68]guideline [ˈɡaɪdlaɪn]n. 规定，准则；指导方针 例 Our guideline is to complement each other's advantages.
[01:41.40]mature [məˈtʃʊə(r)]a. 成熟的；充分考虑的；(票据等)到 期的；成年人的 v. 成熟；到期
[01:47.40]gloom [ɡluːm]n. 忧郁；阴暗；郁闷 v. (使)忧郁；(使)变 暗 搭 gloom and doom 厄运；对未来的悲观、失望
[01:54.60]illusion [ɪˈluːʒn]n. 幻觉，错觉；幻想；错误的观念或信 仰 例 The capacity to modify the economy proved to be an illusion. 搭 be under the illusion that 错误地以为；对… 抱有幻想
[02:09.24]far-flung [ˌfɑː(r)ˈflʌŋ]a. 遥远的；广泛的；辽阔的 例 All EU countries are now linked by exchanges, markets and supply routes to diverse and far-flung places.
[02:24.24]agribusiness [ˈæɡrɪbɪznəs]n. 农业综合企业，农业综合经营 例 What is the main organisation defect of agribusiness?
[02:34.68]vain [veɪn]a. 徒然的；空虚的；虚荣的；无益的；无 价值的 例 I read the scheme again and again, trying hard to understand what he intended to do but in vain. 搭 in vain 徒劳；无效
[02:49.44]falsehood [ˈfɔːlshʊd]n. 谬误；虚伪；说谎；谎言 搭 tell a falsehood 说谎 / truth and falsehood 真理与谬误
[02:58.20]encounter [ɪnˈkaʊntə(r)]n./v. 遇到，遭到 例 Let the manager know whenever you encounter any difficulty. 搭 encounter opposition 遭遇反对 / encounter with 碰撞；与…相遇
[03:13.80]backhander [ˈbækhændə(r)]n. 贿赂；回扣 例 Walmart has been accused of paying backhanders to speed up the opening of new stores.
[03:26.16]caution [ˈkɔːʃn]n. 谨慎，小心；警告，警戒 vt. 警告；保 证 例 All reports emanating from that country should be treated with caution.
[03:37.92]model [ˈmɒdl]vt. 模仿，模拟；塑造；做…的模型 n. 模 型；型号；样式；模范；样品 例 The company is trying to research and develop a new model.
[03:49.20]porcelain [ˈpɔːsəlɪn]n. 瓷；瓷器 a. 瓷(制)的；精美的
[03:53.64]amorphous [əˈmɔːfəs]a. 无固定形状的，不规则的；无固定 界限的；模糊的；无组织的 例 They are amorphous entities with scant leadership structure or formal process for making decisions.
[04:09.84]bottom [ˈbɒtəm]n. 底部，底层；基础
[04:12.72]gazump [ɡəˈzʌmp]v. 欺诈；抬价敲诈 例 It is common to be gazumped by proprietors during the property boom.
[04:22.56]destocking [ˌdiːˈstɒkɪŋ]n. 缩减储量 例 Destocking by retailers should be to blame for their poor financial results.
[04:33.96]contemplate [ˈkɒntəmpleɪt]v. 深思，细想；注视，凝视 例 Only in extreme circumstances would European leaders contemplate this step.
[04:46.56]entangle [ɪnˈtæŋɡl]vt. 使纠缠；使混乱；使卷入，牵连 例 It's said that the company got entangled in dishonest business dealings. 搭 be entangled in a web of difficulties 陷入重 重困难之中 / entangled affair 纠缠不清的事情 / get entangled with sb. 与某人有牵连
[05:09.00]hysteria [hɪˈstɪəriə]n. 不正常的兴奋；歇斯底里，癔症 例 The hysteria that China might endanger the global economy is overstated.
[05:20.88]pacesetter [ˈpeɪssetə(r)]n. 标兵；先导者；领跑者 例 Beijing has been the pacesetter in implementing tough emission standards over the past decade.
[05:35.04]session [ˈseʃn]n. 会议；讲习会；学期；(从事某项活动 的)集会；一段时间 搭 in session 在开庭；在开会
[05:42.12]nucleus [ˈnjuːkliəs]n. (原子)核；核心，中心 搭 play the role of a nucleus 起核心作用
[05:49.20]zenith [ˈzenɪθ]n. 顶峰，最高点；极盛时期 例 He has not yet reached the zenith of his career. 搭 at the zenith of 在…的最高点；处于…的极盛 时期
[06:00.72]cabin [ˈkæbɪn]n. 船舱，机舱，(飞机、汽车等的)座 舱；货仓 例 All commercial airlines allow a limited number of small pets to fly in the cabin. 搭 cabin access 座舱入口 / cabin class 二等舱 / cabin crew (飞机)客舱服务员
[06:18.96]fitting [ˈfɪtɪŋ]n. 装配；修整；试穿；[pl.]设备；家具； 配件 a. 适合的，恰当的 例 For the owner of the fishery, the government offered him a fitting position in a firm.
[06:33.36]versatile [ˈvɜːsətaɪl]a. 有多种技能的；通用的；多功能的
[06:37.92]anaemic [əˈniːmɪk]a. 无活力的，委顿衰弱的；患贫血的
[06:42.00]alliance [əˈlaɪəns]n. 联盟，联合 例 To reduce the transaction cost, the two enterprises came into an alliance as a result of negotiations. 搭 in alliance with 与…联盟 / make an alliance
[06:59.52]handsome [ˈhænsəm]a. 可观的，相当大的；慷慨的 例 They made a handsome profit on the property.
[07:07.80]clarity [ˈklærəti]n. 清楚，明晰；透明 例 Whatever the screen size, what struck me was not the sharpness of the picture but the clarity of the interface.
[07:22.20]analogy [əˈnælədʒi]v. 类似；类推，类比；比拟 n. 类 似，相似 例 There is a fairly good analogy between foreign exchange markets and stock markets. 搭 by analogy 用类推的方法 / on the analogy of 根据…的类推
[07:39.72]bonanza [bəˈnænzə]n. 大矿囊；富源，财源 a. 兴隆的 例 With the exhaustion of mineral resources, the prospect of finding a bonanza dwindled.
[07:52.56]unregulated [ˌʌnˈreɡjuleɪtɪd]a. 无管理的；不可调节的
[07:57.36]refine [rɪˈfaɪn]vt. 提纯，精炼，精制；改进 例 The engineers in the information technology department spent many months refining the software.
[08:10.92]intense [ɪnˈtens]a. 强烈的，剧烈的；热切的；紧张的； 认真的 例 The competition has become increasingly intense for the youths to enter the best enterprises.
[08:25.08]allay [əˈleɪ]vt. 缓解，减轻(痛苦等)；平息，使缓和 例 The government is seeking to allay people's fears of economic recession.
[08:36.48]addendum [əˈdendəm]n. 附录，附件 例 Any addendum to be agreed in future will be regarded as an integral part of this contract.
[08:48.48]exchange [ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ]n. 交换；兑换；外汇；兑换率 vi. 兑 换；交换 搭 cultural exchange 文化交流 / in exchange for 作为对…的交换
[08:58.68]upheaval [ʌpˈhiːvl]n. 剧变；隆起；举起 搭 social upheaval 社会的大变动
[09:04.56]restrict [rɪˈstrɪkt]vt. 限制，约束，约定 搭 be restricted in/to 被限制在…范围内
[09:11.28]biennial [baɪˈeniəl]a. 两年一次的；持续两年的 例 The biennial art show which is held in the city is liked by the people.
[09:22.08]singular [ˈsɪŋɡjələ(r)]a. 非凡的；卓越的；独个的 搭 man of singular courage 胆略超群的人
[09:29.52]access [ˈækses]n. (使用…的)机会或权利；进入…的方 法 vt. 接近，进入；找到(信息) 例 If you can find some data that is reliable and that few other people have access to, you can probably create some very valuable setups for your trading. 搭 access to... 使用…的机会或权利；进入…的 方法 / gain access to 成功进入
[09:55.92]tactic [ˈtæktɪk]n. 战术，策略 例 Trade barriers are in fact a delaying tactic rather than a real solution.
[10:06.00]brisk [brɪsk]a. 生意兴隆的；兴旺的；敏锐的；活泼的 vt. 使活泼 例 Business is always brisk before Christmas. 搭 brisk up 使有生气 / brisk up one's pace 加 快步伐
[10:18.96]remainder [rɪˈmeɪndə(r)]n. 残余物；廉价出售的图书；剩余 财产 vt. 减价出售；削价处理
[10:25.32]grovel [ˈɡrɒvl] vi. 卑躬屈膝；趴，匍匐；沉湎，沉溺 例 To bring the company out of the red, he has to grovel to the bank manager for a loan.
[10:37.32]veterinary [ˈvetrənəri] a. 兽医的
[10:40.56]well-advised [ˌwelədˈvaɪzəd]a. 经周密考虑的；稳妥的；明智 的
[10:45.72]empirical [ɪmˈpɪrɪkl]a. 以经验(或观察)为依据的，经验主义 的；来自经验的 例 We get the conclusion after a lot of empirical research. 搭 empirical average 经验平均值 / empirical evidence 经验性证据 / empirical knowledge 从 实际经验得来的知识
[11:05.88]evidence [ˈevɪdəns]n. 证据，凭证；迹象；明显 例 There is much evidence to show that the financial crisis has passed. 搭 in evidence 明显的，显而易见的 / show evidences of 有…的迹象
[11:21.48]notarise [ˈnəʊtəraɪz]vt. 证明；公证 例 No notary office would notarise this contract as the contents of it are against the law.
[11:33.72]headquarters [ˌhedˈkwɔːtəz]n. (机构、企业等的)总部，总店 例 The company's headquarters are based in Hong Kong.
[11:44.04]mingle [ˈmɪŋɡl]vi. 混合；结合；交往，来回应酬 vt. 使混 合 例 You'd better mingle with the colleagues who can help you get ahead. 搭 mingle with 和…混合；加入 / with mingled feelings 百感交集地
[12:00.36]neutral [ˈnjuːtrəl]a. 中立的；中性的；中立国的 n. 中立 者；中立国 例 Keeping a neutral monetary stance is helpful to maintain rapid economic growth.
[12:13.56]radical [ˈrædɪkl]a. 根本的，彻底的；基本的；激进的
[12:17.52]cash [kæʃ]n. 现金 v. 兑现
[12:19.56]prudent [ˈpruːdnt]a. 谨慎的；判断力强的；(尤指)有利害 关系的
[12:24.24]framework [ˈfreɪmwɜːk]n. 构架，框架；参照标准，准则； 构成方式，体系 例 The government has created the framework for a normal foreign exchange market. 搭 framework of society 社会结构 / metal framework 金属框架
[12:42.72]workfare [ˈwɜːkfeə(r)]n. 工作福利；工作福利制
[12:46.68]gigantic [dʒaɪˈɡæntɪk]a. 巨人似的；巨大的，庞大的 例 Their firm is extremely competitive since they have both highly qualified talents and a gigantic and very refined apparatus.
[13:03.72]negligible [ˈneɡlɪdʒəbl]a. 可以忽略的；不予重视的 例 Domestic tourism demand's contribution to the economic growth is estimated to be negligible.
[13:17.76]berth [bɜːθ]n. 停泊处，泊位 例 The ship went slowly through the dock to the ship berth. 搭 give a wide berth to (为安全或谨慎起见)远 离；对…敬而远之
[13:30.00]dominant [ˈdɒmɪnənt]a. (市场)主导地位的；占优势的；支 配的 例 If China hopes to build dominant names in the global consumer market, then it needs a very different role model.
[13:45.96]outplacement [ˈaʊtpleɪsmənt]n. (被解雇后的)新职介绍
[13:50.76]soar [sɔː(r)]vi. 猛增，剧增 n. 高涨；高飞；上升高度 例 House prices soared a further 20 percent last month.
[14:00.00]outsell [ˌaʊtˈsel]vt. 比…销售得快；卖得比…多 例 According to the statistics, digital cameras will outsell film cameras this year.
[14:12.36]module [ˈmɒdjuːl]n. 单元，单位；模块，组件；(宇宙飞 船上各个独立的)舱
[14:17.52]idealise [aɪˈdiːəlaɪz]v. (使)理想化 例 I don't want to idealise my work.
[14:24.36]survey [ˈsɜːveɪ]n. 测量；调查；检验 [səˈveɪ]vt. 调查；勘测 搭 make a survey of 对…作全面调查 / under survey 在检验中
[14:33.72]circulate [ˈsɜːkjəleɪt]v. (使)流通，(使)周转 例 The big problem arising from LLP must be the creditor protection.
[14:44.64]annuity [əˈnjuːəti]n. 年金，养老金 例 While you wait for it to bounce back, annuity rates could fall.
[14:54.12]built-in [ˌbɪltˈɪn]a. 内置的，嵌入的；内在的；固有的；必 要的 n. 内置 例 The built-in sensors of these shoes can communicate with a runner's iPod to track calorie consumption.
[15:09.84]emission [iˈmɪʃn]n. (纸币等的)发行；发行额；散发(物)， 发射(物) 例 The government decided to increase the emission of the banknotes.
